   "n": 2,
   "via": ".asSequence()",
   "citation": "kotlin-docs-sequences#sequence",
   "why": "A sequence sends one element at a time through `filter` and `map`, and nothing runs until `toList()`. Once the result reaches the size that `take` asks for, the processing stops, so the remaining elements, if any, are never visited."
